## Setting the mod name and version

The file select menu shows your mod's name and version. Set them in `dx/config.h`:

```c
#define DX_MOD_NAME "My Cool Mod"
#define DX_MOD_VER_MAJOR 1
#define DX_MOD_VER_MINOR 0
#define DX_MOD_VER_PATCH 0
```

When you create a mod, Diorama64 sets `DX_MOD_NAME` to the name you enter. The mod name can be up to 27 characters.

## Skipping the intro and demo

These settings in `dx/config.h` skip scenes that play on their own, which saves time while you test:

| Setting | Default | What it skips when `1` |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `DX_SKIP_LOGOS` | `0` | The logo screens, such as the Nintendo and Intelligent Systems logos |
| `DX_SKIP_STORY` | `1` | The opening storybook |
| `DX_SKIP_DEMO` | `1` | The demo reel that plays if the player waits at the title screen |

To show players the full intro and demo, set `DX_SKIP_LOGOS`, `DX_SKIP_STORY`, and `DX_SKIP_DEMO` to `0` before you release your mod.

## Replacing the title screen images

The title screen draws these images, from `mapfs/title/`:

| File | What it shows | Size |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `logotype.png` | The Paper Mario logo | 200 × 112 |
| `press_start.png` | The "PRESS START" text, in grayscale with transparency | 128 × 32 |
| `copyright.png` | The copyright notice, in grayscale with transparency | 144 × 32 |

The background behind them is `mapfs/bg/title_bg.png`.

To replace an image, replace its file with your own PNG of the same size.

## Replacing the storybook pictures

The opening storybook uses these images, from `title/`:

| File | What it shows | Size |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `bg_1.png` to `bg_4.png` | The storybook's pictures | 264 × 162 |
| `tape.png` | The storybook's tape | 128 × 128 |
| `bowser_silhouette.png` | Bowser's silhouette | 128 × 128 |

Keep each replacement the same size as the original.
